From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:45:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: debug labels per guest pass and port pass, names on
 the engine's targets

For RenderDoc and the validation layer's messages. On with
PS3RECOMP_VK_LABELS=1, or with PS3RECOMP_VK_VALIDATION=1 unless
PS3RECOMP_VK_LABELS=0, and only when VK_EXT_debug_utils is there (the
instance then enables it without the validation layer). Off, every place
costs one test of a flag, and the engine never builds a name: it asks the
backend once, at init (rsx_draw_backend.debug_enabled).

The draw engine names each guest pass by its target set, in frame order
("pass 3: A 0x0C3A0000 640x360 RGBA8 | Z 0x...") through the optional
debug_pass hook, and each colour and zeta target it makes ("colour
0:0x... 1280x720 RGBA8") through debug_name. A clear looks the zeta up
without making one, so names never change what the engine allocates.
The backend opens a region around the Vulkan render passes of a guest
pass, and around its own passes: jm_post's MLAA and motion blur on the
GPU, the temporal upscaler (DLSS, FSR 3.1), FSR 1 and the present. A
region is opened only on a command buffer being recorded and closed in
the same function, so begin and end always pair. Written from the Vulkan
specification.
